{"clock":34,"ops":[{"kind":"link","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"71995850419c2e2fdfc09ea4800d52caad3de8f7","forge_id":"5978901142","number":"45","url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/45"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"71995850419c2e2fdfc09ea4800d52caad3de8f7","field":"title","value":"ci: make ci runs everything CI runs, and lefthook runs the fast checks on each commit"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"71995850419c2e2fdfc09ea4800d52caad3de8f7","field":"body","value":"\u003c!-- git-bug:0aa3715278563e1a807ff6e75bba390e12ae2d868086a41d2fbdbd1d5ae5fd6f --\u003e\n`make ci` skips the web checks: they are written out in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (npm ci, typecheck, test, build), so a local `make ci` isn't the CI and CLAUDE.md has to list them apart. Lint, format and type-check should always run locally (the user, 2026-10-21), as co2-calculator's lefthook does.\n\nADR 0001 (docs/adr/0001-check-results-are-signed-git-notes.md) makes the local run the proof; the cycle protocol's M4 proposes `[cycle.checks]` from lefthook's pre-commit. This gives it a real one to read.\n\n\n- `make ci` runs the web checks and build too, and installs web dependencies only when the lockfile changed.\n- `ci.yml` sets up Go and Node, then runs `make ci`, and nothing else.\n- A `lefthook.yml` pre-commit runs gofmt, go vet and the web typecheck, each only when matching files are staged. No pre-push hook: wtx's push guard owns it.\n- lefthook is pinned and installed by one documented command.\n- CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and README say `make ci` alone."}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"71995850419c2e2fdfc09ea4800d52caad3de8f7","field":"status","value":"closed"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"71995850419c2e2fdfc09ea4800d52caad3de8f7","field":"labels","value":"kind:chore\nprio:p2\nstatus:done"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"71995850419c2e2fdfc09ea4800d52caad3de8f7","field":"assignees","value":"161889"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"71995850419c2e2fdfc09ea4800d52caad3de8f7","field":"comment:6343273836","value":"\u003c!-- git-bug:e2cd1d1aa5bf60e63d667f3e716e6646a5ab412ce0e8276f5fbf625e89552273 --\u003e\nLanded in #41 (merge 45dca2d). `make ci` runs the web checks and build too, `ci.yml` only sets up Go and Node and runs `make ci`, and `lefthook.yml` runs gofmt, go vet and the web typecheck at pre-commit. lefthook is pinned by the `tool` line in `go.mod`; install it once per clone with `go tool lefthook install`."}}]}